{
  "events": [
    {
      "id": "6397",
      "name": "Ctrl PDX: Rumble by the Railroad",
      "url": "https://www.robotcombatevents.com/events/6397",
      "start_date": "01/10/2026",
      "end_date": "01/10/2026",
      "location": "Portland, OR, United States",
      "bots_count": 55,
      "logo_url": "https://robotcombatevents.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/event/logo/6397/ctrl_pdx_rce_logo_1-10_3x.png",
      "description": "Join our Discord for more info! https://discord.gg/FcuCNv2ug2\n\nDoor Code: 03834\n\nWelcome to CTRL PDX! Rumble at the Railroad is our fourth event, and we’re super excited, with a prize pool of over $700! Spectators and competitors of any skill level are welcome! Bot check-in starts at 9 and brackets will be created at 11. If possible, please arrive with your bot ready to pass safety and compete.\n\nThank you to our sponsors who have generously offered prizes for each of the competing brackets! Thank you to Turnabot, Polymaker, Fingertech Robotics, and Just 'Cuz Robotics for their support. Please check out their websites below to learn more.\n\nTurnabot \n\nPolymaker US Store\n\nFingertech Robotics\n\nJust 'Cuz Robotics\n\n\nSchedule:\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t9:00 - 11:00\n\t\t\tCheck in and safety\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t10:30 - 11:00\n\t\t\tDriver's meeting\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t11:00 - 1:45 \n\t\t\tFights\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t1:45 - 2:30\n\t\t\tLunch break\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2:30 - 5:30\n\t\t\tFights Resume!\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t5:30 - 6:30\n\t\t\tTeardown\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\nThe schedule is a loose esimate of how the day will go. Things are subject to change.\n\nSafety: To pass safety, your bot will need to be weighed and demonstrate that it can failsafe. For safety purposes, if a robot’s battery is exposed to its opponent, that robot will lose the fight. In the event of a lipo puncture or fire, we will have a lipo bucket with kitty litter and tongs, as well as someone nearby who can run the bucket out of the building. \n\nArena: We have a 4-foot by 4-foot box with an untreated steel floor. There may be a hazard, which would be a shelf that bots could push their opponents onto to demonstrate control, however their opponents would be able to easily escape. We are still deciding wheather or not to add this. There will not be a pit of any kind. Join the discord to let us know your thoughts!\n\nRules: We will be using the standard Sparc ruleset for full-class metal antweight, plastic antweight, and fairyweight. We are allowing the weight bonuses outlined in the Sparc ruleset for plastic antweight and fairyweight classes only, in the interest of arena safety. Fights are 3 minutes long.\n\nFighting Format: The tournament will use a modified double elimination bracket. If a weight class has less than 6 robots, we will do a round-robin tournament for that weight class.Our weight classes and maximum class sizes are:\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFairyweight\n\t\t\t16 bots\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFull Combat Ant\n\t\t\t24 bots\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tPlastic Ant\n\t\t\t24 bots\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\nWe have expanded the Fairyweight bracket from 12 robots to 16 to help support the larger demand. As of right now, we will not be expanding any weight classes to make sure we finish on time.\n\n\nPrizes: For each weight class the respective finish will recieve the following:\n\nFirst:\n\nFull-Metal Antweight:\n\n\n\t$50 gift card to Turnabot\n\t$50 gift card to Fingertech Robotics\n\t1kg of Polyflex TPU90\n\tJust 'Cuz Long All-In-One PD Board\n\n\nPlastic Antweight:\n\n\n\t$50 gift card to Turnabot\n\t$50 gift card to Fingertech Robotics\n\t1kg of Polylite PLA Pro\n\tJust 'Cuz Long All-In-One PD Board\n\n\nFairyweight:\n\n\n\t$50 gift card to Turnabot\n\t$20 gift card to Fingertech Robotics\n\t1kg of Polylite PLA Pro\n\t2 Just 'Cuz Micro PD Boards\n\n\nSecond: \n\nFull Metal Antweight:\n\n\n\t$30 gift card to Turnabot\n\t$25 gift card to Fingertech Robotics\n\t1kg of Polylite PLA Pro\n\n\nPlastic Antweight:\n\n\n\t$30 gift card to Turnabot\n\t$25 gift card to Fingertech Robotics\n\t1kg of Polylite PLA Pro\n\n\nFairyweight:\n\n\n\t$30 gift card to Turnabot\n\t$10 gift card to Fingertech Robotics\n\t1kg of Polylite PLA Pro\n\tJust 'Cuz Micro PD Board\n\n\nThird: \n\nFull Metal Antweight:\n\n\n\t$20 gift card to Turnabot\n\t$10 gift card to Fingertech Robotics\n\n\nPlastic Antweight:\n\n\n\t$20 gift card to Turnabot\n\t$10 gift card to Fingertech Robotics\n\n\nFairyweight:\n\n\n\t$20 gift card to Turnabot\n\tJust 'Cuz Micro PD Board\n\n\n\nEntrance Fee: Builders will be charged a $20 entry fee per robot. This is to offset the cost of our box, improve builder experience, and to purchase other materials. A portion of this money will also go to the event space. You can pay at the event or ahead of time in cash or here on the RCE website. If you cannot pay this fee, please let us know and accomodations can be made.\n\nEntry to the building: There are two ways to get inside; through a back door (the code is 03834) and a short path inside the building to our space, or through the front entrance on Baltimore Ave, up the stairs, and look for room 212 on the map. The back door comes up when you search  6700 N New York Ave in Google Maps, or as 9010 N Decatur St on Apple Maps. More information on how to get to the event space can be found on our discord.",
      "competitions": [
