    {
      "id": "6334",
      "name": "The Bot Spot: Winter Wreckage",
      "url": "https://www.robotcombatevents.com/events/6334",
      "start_date": "01/17/2026",
      "end_date": "01/17/2026",
      "location": "Provo, UT, United States",
      "bots_count": 47,
      "logo_url": "https://robotcombatevents.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/event/logo/6334/Resized_1758307348141_b.jpeg",
      "description": "Welcome to The Bot Spot! \n\nThis Tournament will host Beetle, FC Ant, Plastic Ant, and Fairyweight brackets. \n\nAddress: 255 N University Ave, Provo, UT 84604\n\nDetails \u0026 Links:\n\n\n\tLunch \u0026 snacks will be available for purchase \n\tPower Outlets will be available\n\tTournament will be live-streamed on YouTube: \n\t\n\t\ttbd\n\t\n\t\n\tChallonge brackets:\n\t\n\t\tFairyweight: challonge.com/tbswwfairy\n\t\tPlastic Ant:   challonge.com/tbswwplant\n\t\tFC Ant:         challonge.com/tbswwant\n\t\tBeetle:          challonge.com/tbswwbeetle\n\t\n\t\n\n\nSchedule:\n\n\n\t8:00am: Doors open\n\t8:30am: Safety Inspections begin\n\t9:30am: Safety Inspections end\n\t9:45am: Driver's Safety Meeting\n\t10:00am: Brackets are shuffled and finalized\n\t10:05am: Fights begin!\n\tLunch: 60 minute break sometime around 12 or 1\n\tFighting resumes; tournament ends around 5:00pm (loose estimate)\n\n\n\nTournament Rules:\n\n\n\tAll brackets will follow SPARC guidelines v1.5. Judges will use the \"Damage, Agression, \u0026 Control\" criteria \n\tBrackets with 7+ players will be double elimination. Brackets with 6 or less will be round-robin brackets\n\n\nAdditional Rules:\n\n\n\tAll batteries MUST be charged in a fireproof bag or container. Participants who break this rule will be asked to leave.\n\tBeetleweight weapons will be limited to 250mph tip speed in order to minimize arena damage. The Event Organizer will reach out to each Beetle participant (where applicable) prior to the event. Tip speed will be calculated theorhetically using the following: Weapon Radius, Pulley Ratio (if applicable), Motor kv Rating, and LiPo Cell Count. (LiPo: 4.2V/cell. LiHv: 4.35V/cell, unless charged to 4.2V). \n\tEach robot must be able to fit in a 1ft cube (in any orientation). This is done to ensure that if a bot is on fire it can fit in the sand bucket. Flexible parts that can easily be manipulated to fit are allowed\n\tMagnets for dowforce are allowed (except for Plastic Antweight). The robot cannot have enough magnetic force to hang upside down from a steel plate\n\tThroughout the tournament, bots may be weighed before a fight to ensure fair play\n\tEach bot is guarunteed 20 min of repair time between fights. Bots who need more repair time will be given an additional 20 minutes, but will forfeit the next match should it end with a judge's decision. (Limit once per bot)\n\n\nSafety Inspections:\n\n\n\tEach robot willl be weighed (For modular robots, weigh in with your heaviest configuration)\n\tEach robot will be inspected to ensure it follows SPARC build guidelines\n\tThe robot will be placed in the arena to demonstrate safe Load In \u0026 Load Out procedure, and failsafes for weapon and drive systems\n\n\nArena Details:\n\n\n\tArena is 8 x 8 x 4ft in size\n\tFloor material is steel\n\n\nWe ask that every participant include a photo of their robot in the robot's profile. No mysterious competitors!\n\nEvent Organizer:\nJohn Hellewell: hellewell.johnr@gmail.com\nPlease reach out to me with any questions",
