    {
      "id": "6367",
      "name": "Winter Wars 2026 - MRCA Qualifier and Coat Drive event",
      "url": "https://www.robotcombatevents.com/events/6367",
      "start_date": "01/17/2026",
      "end_date": "01/17/2026",
      "location": "Doniphan, MO, United States",
      "bots_count": 67,
      "logo_url": "https://robotcombatevents.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/event/logo/6367/Messenger_creation_D64F2A59-E0D6-4031-8C33-EC79FF3B15FC.png",
      "description": "❄️ WINTER WARS IS BACK! ❄️\nCombat Robots \u0026 Coat Drive – Year 3\n\nWe’re excited to announce the return of Winter Wars, our Combat Robots and Coat Drive event, now in its 3rd year!\n⭐ This will be the FIRST MRCA event of 2026!\nLast year we gave away over $1,500 in prizes, and we’re hoping to match (or beat!) that again this year.\n\n\n📅 Event Details\nDate: January 17, 2026\nLocation:\n📍 506 Pine St., Doniphan, MO 63935\nSEMO Combat Robotics Headquarters\n\n• MRCA Qualifier Event\n• 2 Arenas\n• Classes: Plastic Ant, Ant, Beetleweight\n• MRCA ruleset enforced\n👉 https://midwestrobotcombat.com/rules/\n(No weight bonus of any kind)\n\n\n🧥 BONUS EVENTS\n\n1. COAT DRIVE CONTEST – 1st Place wins an autographed Rusty Plush\nShow Us Your Warmest Bot!\nShow your creativity and support the coat drive with a winter- or coat-themed robot.\n• Decorated, painted, or themed (Winter, Christmas, or Coat Drive)\n• Each bot displayed with a donation jar\n• Audience may walk through pits to vote by donating\n• Bot with the most donations wins a bonus prize\n• All proceeds go toward the coat drive\n• Recommended to decorate your clone (judging occurs after all first-round matches)\n(Yes… a fighting boot may make an appearance 😄)\n\n2. Abby’s Brace Send-Off\nA single-round event for any 1 lb bot that wants to participate. Abby has competed with SEMO at several events and, after overcoming major medical challenges, no longer needs her brace. She has asked for a send-off by placing the brace in the arena and letting the bots attack it.\n• Each bot will have a balloon attached\n• Last balloon popped wins a prize\n\n3. King of the Hill\n• Antweight and Beetleweight\n• 3-minute rounds\n• Winner is the bot on the center block when time expires\n• Match stops immediately if a battery is exposed for safe removal\n\n\n🕗 Event Schedule\n• 8:00 AM – Doors open / Registration begins\n– Pick up waiver and contract at registration\n– Complete and return forms to receive safety sheet\n• 8:00 – 9:30 AM – Safety checks\n– Weapon and drive failsafe testing required\n– Failsafes must function to pass safety (check prior to arrival)\n– Waiver must be signed before safety check\n• 9:30 – 10:00 AM – Final arena checks (staff only)\n– Brackets posted on on-site TV, Facebook, YouTube, and Challonge\n• 10:00 AM – Driver meeting\n• 10:30 AM – Fights begin\n• 1:00 PM – Lunch break (~1 hour)\n– Kitchen menu posted closer to event date\n• ~5:30 PM – Event wrap-up (may run slightly past)\n\n\n🏨 Lodging\nRecommended Hotel: Rocky River Inn\n📞 573-996-2400\n📍 100 Oak Tree Village, Doniphan, MO 63935\n(Approx. 1 mile from event center)\nAirBNBs also available nearby with good feedback.\n\n\n🔗 Helpful Links\n• Facebook Group: https://www.facebook.com/share/g/1GofrkpLoR/\n• Discord: https://discord.gg/MpxbDX3C",
