    {
      "id": "6464",
      "name": "Winter Wars '26",
      "url": "https://www.robotcombatevents.com/events/6464",
      "start_date": "01/24/2026",
      "end_date": "01/24/2026",
      "location": "Corvallis, OR, United States",
      "bots_count": 20,
      "logo_url": "https://robotcombatevents.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/event/logo/6464/IMG_1865.JPG",
      "description": "Hosted by DAM Robotics club and open to the public, Winter Wars '26 is Oregon State University's second robot combat competition of this academic year! Oregon State Combat Robotics (OSCR) is a branch of DAM Robotics club, where members learn the basics of combat robotics through a basic curriculum and hands-on design by developing their own Plastic Antweight robots. Now is the time to test ourselves against others in the Combat Robotics community!\n\nWinter Wars '26 will take place on Saturday, January 24th in Oregon State University's Kelley Engineering Center atrium with doors opening at 10:00 am and fights starting by 11:30 am.\n\n \n\nExact schedule is subject to change, though it will look pretty close to this:\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t10:00am - 11:00am\n\t\t\tSafety\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t11:00am - 11:30am\n\t\t\tBuilders meeting / final setup\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t11:30am - ~2:00pm\n\t\t\tFights!\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2:00pm - 2:30pm\n\t\t\tLunch (or repair time for some)\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2:30pm - 6:00pm\n\t\t\tRest of the fights!\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n \n\nOur arena is 6 feet x 6 feet wide and 3 feet tall. The floor is steel with steel kickplates. The floor is painted for grip, though there is not added grip compound. In one corner is a 1 foot square pit which currently is set to always be open. Our pit has a 1 inch tall lip around the outside. This arena is suitable for up to beetleweight robots and now that we have thoroughly tested it (thanks Noob Tube) weight bonuses are allowed following the newly revised Sparc Rules (1.5): https://osurobotics.club/teams/combat/sparc/\n\nOur arena will also be featuring our built in house ready/tapout light system as seen at Spring Skirmish '25, but more durable this time! Each competitor will have access to a green button for readying up and a red button for tapping out which should not be possible to accidentally press. This system will be explained in more detail during the drivers meeting.\n\n \n\nAt this event we will offer:\n\n\n\tFull combat antweight\n\tFairyweight\n\tBeetleweight\n\tPlastic antweight\n\n\nThis tournament, in all weight classes, will be modified double-elimination style with first bracket match winners moving on and losers moving into the second bracket. Losing in the second bracket will knock a bot out of the competition. The winner of the first bracket and the winner of the second bracket will meet in the finals which will be single elimination. If a weightclass has 5 or less bots we will run a round robin bracket instead.\n\n \n\nFinally, club funding is down this year, even more than last year, so to ensure we can continue hosting competitions while also running our club we will have a $10/bot fee. We will be accepting payments on RCE and in-person. We thankfully don't have to pay for our own insurance at this event, but the club costs a lot to run so if you're able we'd really appreciate this.\n\nIf you have any questions, we can answer them in the competitor discord: https://discord.gg/4w64KNZK4U\n\nOSCR events are sponsored by Repeat Robotics, Polymaker, \u0026 OnShape",
      "competitions": [
        {
