    {
      "id": "6465",
      "name": "WINTER WRECKAGE - Impact Robotics League event #2",
      "url": "https://www.robotcombatevents.com/events/6465",
      "start_date": "01/31/2026",
      "end_date": "01/31/2026",
      "location": "Rocklin, CA, United States",
      "bots_count": 86,
      "logo_url": "https://robotcombatevents.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/event/logo/6465/impact-logo.jpg",
      "description": "Impact Robotics League is a new youth combat league for Northern Californa and beyond.\nCurrently Grades 7-12 \n\nFast-paced tournament format with 3 matches guaranteed for every team.  Group play followed up single elimination \n\nRegistration and details are available on the ImpactRoboticsLeague.org website. \n\nSee the  WINTER WRECKAGE Page for complete information on the EDU divisions! (coming soon)\n\n\n\nEvent Details\n\n\n\t\nDate: Saturday, January 31, 2026\n\t\nLocation: Sierra College Campus Cafeteria, Rocklin, CA\n\t\nEntry Fee: $20 per bot\n\tAll bracket are group play preliminary stage, with top 8-16 advancing to single elimination\n\t\nDivisions: \n\t\n\t\tBeginner EDU (grades 7-12*) Impact Robotic League Rules - brushed drive, 3S only\n\t\tIntermediate EDU (grades 7-12*) Impact Robotic League Rules  brushed drive, 3S only\n\t\tAdvanced/Open (all ages)\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\nSPARC 1.6 Construction Rules as the baseline \n\t\t\t\nPlacer Robotics 25-26 Rules  , including changes/deviations from Sparc 1.6. Please see the document for complete details. Major differences include:\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tOriginal Work Expectations (Section 18 addition)\n\t\t\t\tMagnetic Downforce Limits (Section 17 addition \n\t\t\t\tTip Speed Limit 250mph (Section \n\t\t\t\tWeapon restrictions: No Fire, Flamethrowers, Smoke, Pneumatics, Special Weapons, Internal Combustion Engines (ICE) and liquid fuels, etc \n\t\t\t\tPlastic Ants: No TPU as per sparc 1.6 with the sole exception of TPU weapon or drive belts  are permitted as emergency replacements \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n*We do accept 6th grade participants on an case by case basis for EDU divisions  - please contact the event organizer for details. \n\nRegistration Deadlines and Details -\n\n\n\tEDU divisions must also register on ImpactRoboticsLeague.org,\n\n\tOpen teams please register via RCE\n\tOne robot per builder/driver . Large clubs (such as school based programs) may enter multiple bots provided each bot is designed, managed/repaired and driven by a subteam/builder.  Contact the EO to confirm if you have any questions.\n\t\nAdult supervision required onsite for duration of event for anyone under age of 18\n\t\nRegistration Deadline: January 24, 2026\n\t\nPayment Deadline: January 17, 206 . Any team not paid by the deadline will be moved to the waitlist \n\t--\u003e Pay Here\n\tAll participants and supervising adults must complete liability/media release waiver for the season. If you completed the waiver for IRL #1 FALL BRAWL, you do not need to complete it again.  \n\t--\u003e Complete the Online Waiver Here\n\n\n\nWe are excited to announce HAKKO and FingerTech Robotics are providing prizes/swag as League sponsors! \n\n \n\nFriday, January 30 (Optional Check in and Inspection)\n\n\n\t\n6:00 - 8:00 PM — Optional check-in, inspection, and safety\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSaturday, January 31 (Competition)\n\n\n\t\n7:30 AM — Venue opens to teams\n\t\n8:00 AM — Venue opens to public\n\t\n8:30 AM — Check-in \u0026 safety deadline\n\t\n9:00 AM — Fights begin!\n\t\n12:00 PM — Lunch break\n\t\n12:45 PM — Fights resume\n\t\n4:00 - 5:00 PM — Finals, awards, cleanup (estimated)\n\n\nSee the IRL Compete page for:\n\n\n\tSafety Rules\n\tTournament Rules\n\tConstruction Rules for the Beginner and Intermediate divisions",
