    {
      "id": "6467",
      "name": "TECH CENTER TAKE DOWN",
      "url": "https://www.robotcombatevents.com/events/6467",
      "start_date": "01/31/2026",
      "end_date": "01/31/2026",
      "location": "Norman, OK, United States",
      "bots_count": 47,
      "logo_url": "https://robotcombatevents.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/event/logo/6467/TECH.jpg",
      "description": "Start out the new Year fighting bots in Oklahoma!   We will be fighting 1 pound Ant Full combat bots and Plants,  3D printed bots.\n\n \n\nRobots:  Robots must meet the SPARC Robot Construction Specifications.  We will not allow pneumatics, hydraulics, ICE (Internal Combustion Engines), or  FIRE.  No sportsman categories so no need to worry about rules in that section. (i.e. no limits on weapon tip speed). \n\nPlastic Ants   Again, please review the SPARC Robot Construction Specifications. There is a section for plants at the end of the document.  The body and weapon must be 3D printed.  Several plastics are allowed but No TPU anywhere on the robot. \n\nDriver Limit 2 bots per person, 1 in each weight class.  This rule might be relaxed in the last week before fight day.\n\nTournament Format   \n\nWe will start with a qualifying bracket and then a single elimination bracket.  2 minute rounds. Bots that survive 2 minutes will go to judges decision.  \n\nRound 1 8 fights. Brackets will be randomized when registration closes.\n\nRound 2  8 fights.  All bots that win round 1 will fight each other,  all bots that lose in round 1 will fight each other.  Bots that win, 2-0 will qualify  Bots that lose 0-2 will be done competing for the day. Bots that are 1-1 will move on to round 3.\n\nRound 3 4 fights.  All bots with 1 win 1 loss record. All bots that win (2-1) will qualify, losing bots will be done for the day (1-2) \n\nWe will begin the single elimination bracket with 2-0 bots fighting 1-1 record bots.  Brackets will be arrange to prevent repeat match ups. Bots that make it to semi-final round will fight to determine 3rd place \n\n \n\nPodium \n\n1st, 2nd, 3rd place trophies for each category.\n\n \n\nSponsorships\n\n We hope to have gift cards or merchandise for all 3 podium finishes.  Our goal is to add sponsors in this section and have drawings for prizes.\n\nIf you wish to donate, contact event organizer at email below. \n\n \n\nSafety Considerations\n\n A LiPo charging bag must be used when charging your batteries. \n\nWeapon locks and sharp edge covers must be used while the bot is outside of the arena.\n\nBot drive can be tested in pit area if wheels are supported off the table with weapon lock in place or weapon removed.\n\nAll bot testing with weapon must be in test box or arena.\n\nSafety glasses when using power tools.\n\n \n\nLocation: \n\nThis is an indoor event at the Moore Norman Technology Center Franklin  Road Campus 4701 12th Avenue NW Norman, OK 73069\n\nEntry will be at the southern most of building facing west towards 12th avenue NW,   Gate # 5.  Entry door is locked at all times, we will have volunteers stationed to open door hopefully to end of day,  But phone numbers will be posted if you are not able to enter.\n\n \n\nFacilities: \n\n Event will be held in the Engineering room.  Space is limited. Tables are standing height.  Additional tables will be in hall way just outside room. \n\nWe will do our best to have power at each table.  Lipo charging will most likely be in 1 centralized location. \n\n \n\nSchedule: \n\n8:00 - Doors open and check in and Safety begins\n\n09:45 - Safety Ends, must pass safety to be in tournament\n\n09:45 - Drivers meeting, bracket created\n\n10:00 - Fights begin\n\n12:30 – Break for lunch PIZZA\n\n13:00 - Fighting resumes\n\n17:00 - Estimated wrap up time\n\n \n\nArena:\n\nMain Arena is 8x8x4 with wood floor. Walls are 2 polycarbonate panels 0.25 inch thick with airgap between.\n\nBeetles and Full Combat ants, and  plastic ants are safe to operate.\n\nSecondary arena is 8x4x2 wooden arena with one layer of polycarbonate which can be used for safety and possible matches with plastic ants.\n\nFees: Competitors  will be charge $20 per bot.  And $5 for pizza lunch.\n\n \n\nJoin our Discord and Facebook groups for more updates!\n\nDiscord Server https://discord.gg/GzpqxbHyXa\n\nFacebook: Combat Robots of Oklahoma",
      "competitions": [
