    {
      "id": "6475",
      "name": "Presented By The Hewitt School: Big Apple Bash",
      "url": "https://www.robotcombatevents.com/events/6475",
      "start_date": "01/31/2026",
      "end_date": "01/31/2026",
      "location": "New York, NY, United States",
      "bots_count": 20,
      "logo_url": "https://www.robotcombatevents.com/assets/RCELogo-3383ca77f76e5be2b7755ea9d0c464aea25a87d8c9f2a4cffd63643392f59fe7.png",
      "description": "THE HEWITT SCHOOL — BIG APPLE BASH\n\n\nWe are thrilled to announce Big Apple Bash, Hewitt’s first official combat robotics event, showcasing competitive engineering, creative design, and community collaboration.\n\n📅 Date: Saturday, January 31, 2026\n📍 Location: The Hewitt School — Upper East Side, NYC\n🔧 Competition Class: Antweight Robots (1 lb)\n🏆 Divisions: Youth \u0026 Adult Brackets (now combined)\n📐 Rule Set: SPARC.IO Competition Rules\n\n\n⚙️ Division Details\n\nFor this event, the Youth and Adult brackets have been combined, meaning:\n\n\n\t\n\tYouth and Adult competitors will face each other in matches.\n\t\n\t\n\tMatches will rotate between competitors from both age groups, ensuring everyone gets a fair and exciting mix of opponents.\n\t\n\t\n\tAt the end of the event, finals and awards will be presented based on overall performance, not age division.\n\t\n\n\nPrizes:\n🥇 1st Place – Combat Winner\n🥈 2nd Place – Combat Winner\n🥉 3rd Place – Combat Winner\n👗 Special Prize – High Fashion Robot Contest Winner\n\n\n\t\n\t \n\t\n\n\n🔧 Combat Rules (SPARC.IO Standard)\n\nAll robots must follow SPARC.IO rules and Hewitt safety protocols.\n\n❗ Strictly Prohibited Weapon Types\n\n\n\t\n\tOverhead attacks (hammer-saw mechanisms; note: hammers are allowed)\n\t\n\t\n\tFlamethrowers or fire-based systems\n\t\n\t\n\tTasers, stun weapons, or high-voltage discharge\n\t\n\t\n\tRadio jamming or signal interference\n\t\n\t\n\tEntanglement weapons (ropes, nets, wires, adhesives, foams, tethers, or anything designed to immobilize a robot)\n\t\n\n\nRobots using banned systems will not be allowed to compete.\n\n\n🛡️ Safety \u0026 Inspection\n\nAll robots must pass a mandatory inspection before entering the arena:\n\n✔️ Weapon failsafe functions properly\n✔️ Drive system failsafe works\n✔️ Battery is enclosed and undamaged\n✔️ All sharp/exposed components are shielded in the pit\n✔️ Transport locks are used when moving the robot\n\nRobots failing inspection cannot compete until corrected.\n\n\n👗✨ High Fashion Robot Contest\n\nBecause New York robotics deserves runway-level style!\n\n\n\t\n\tDress your robot in the most stylish, creative, or outrageous outfit\n\t\n\t\n\tFashion elements must be cosmetic only (no weapon activation)\n\t\n\t\n\tRobots will be judged for creativity, design, and presentation\n\t\n\n\nWinner receives a special event award!\n\n\n🕒 Tentative Schedule\n\n\n\t\n\t8:00 AM — Doors Open / Registration\n\t\n\t\n\t8:30–10:00 AM — Robot Safety Inspections\n\t\n\t\n\t10:00 AM — Driver \u0026 Competitor Meeting\n\t\n\t\n\t10:30 AM — Matches Begin\n\t\n\t\n\t1:00 PM — Lunch Break\n\t\n\t\n\t5:00–5:30 PM — Finals \u0026 Awards\n\t\n\n\n\nContact Us:\n📧 Andrew.Iacona@hewittschool.org\n📞 212-288-1919 ext. 390",
