      "logo_url": "https://robotcombatevents.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/event/logo/6496/g151.png",
      "description": "Richmond Area Bot Instigated Destruction is pleased to announce our next event: Cupid Carnage!\n\nWe are running our 6ft x 6ft antweight arena and our 4ft x 4ft fairy arena!\n\nSpectators: The event is free to spectators and no tickets are required! Robot matches will begin around 11AM. Matches typically go till 6pm, but the most action happens at the beginning because there are more back to back matches.\n\nPits will be inside, but you may need to bring your own extension cords, and power strips. Please use a lipo bag while charging. We will be posting updates on our discord server, feel free to join us: https://discord.gg/H5wQnJXAVh\n\nIf you know anyone who would like to volunteer at our events, please have them email us or reach out on discord! We are a 501(c)(3) organization and are willing to sign off for volunteer hours.\n\n \n\nA Huge thanks to our sponsors that make this event possible!\n\nItgresa\n\nRepeat Robotics\n\nRoach Robotics\n\nTurnabot\n\nNumakers Filament\n\nPolymaker\n\nCAD Class Use code RABIDRVA at checkout for 10% off anything in the CAD Class catalog!\n\n \n\nLOCATION:\n\nWe are pleased to announce our location for this event! A big thanks to Regency Mall giving us a space to host this event!\n\nRegency Mall\n\n1420 N Parham Rd\n\nRichmond, VA 23229 \n\nOn the lower level, the central common area right outside the Adult Education Center.\n\n \n\nTimes:\n\n9:00am Doors and pits open\n\n9:45am Safety and checkin\n\n10:30am Drivers meeting, safety closed\n\n11:00am FIGHTS START\n\n \n\n \n\nClass:\n\nPlastic antweights\n\nFull Combat Antweights\n\nFairyweights (150g)\n\n \n\nPrizes:\n\nTBD\n\n \n\nRules:\n\nWe will follow modified SPARC rulesets for both classes. Download the rules here!\n\nApproved materials for plastic ants are printed PET, PETG, ABS, ASA, PLA, PLA+, and TPU.\n\n -Motors, wheels, fasteners, and electronics do not need to be printed, but must not be a significant structural part of the bot.\n\n -Any non printed parts should not be exposed in a way that they can be hit, or hit another bot. The bot should be as much 3d printed as possible.\n\n \n\nNo heat, fire, smoke, entanglement, or other weapons that do not fit the spirit of the rules.\n\nShufflers will get a 1.25x bonus (568g ant and plant, 188g fairy)\n\nNon-traditional locomotion will get 1.5x weight bonus. Ex. Gyro Walkers/Bristle Bots (681g ant and plant, 225g fairy)\n\nTrue walkers using no continuous rotational movement for locomotion (this includes things like vibration motors) will get a full weight bonus (908g ant and plant, 300g fairy)\n\nBatteries should be protected at all times. If a battery becomes exposed during the fight, the match is over. The bot with the exposed battery loses. Take care when charging batteries and charge them in lipo bags.\n\nBots will be given at least 20 minutes between fights for repairs. Later in the day, we may need to be strict on this time, so please work with us.\n\nThere will only be 1 attempt at an unstick and only if both bots are stuck. If they cannot be unstuck or get stuck again, the match will go to the judges.\n\nIf you have any rules questions, please contact us BEFORE the event.\n\n \n\nFormat:\n\nDouble elimination bracket\n\n2:30 minute matches\n\n \n\n \n\nIf you have any questions, feel free to email us at rabidrva@gmail.com or chat on discord https://discord.gg/H5wQnJXAVh",
      "competitions": [
