    {
      "id": "6527",
      "name": "Test and tune up",
      "url": "https://www.robotcombatevents.com/events/6527",
      "start_date": "02/21/2026",
      "end_date": "02/21/2026",
      "location": "Wichita, KS, United States",
      "bots_count": 11,
      "logo_url": "https://robotcombatevents.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/event/logo/6527/IMG_20250514_130806.jpg",
      "description": "Bring your bot and have it figth as many times as you want or can.\n\nIs almost the beginning  of the season and there is more events every time, so let's just meet in the middle  of the country and test your bots with as many driver as you can. \n\nThe event is to learn and prepare.\n\nIn a regular event you have time lines for fix ups, knowing  what are your capabilities  to be ready for the next fight, or learn the weak spots on your bot in a real fight is important. \n\nAlso learn how functional is your weapon, the speed on your drive, how effective  is your defensive system, and over all how fun this is when the pressure  doesn't exist.\n\nThe rules for safety are as every event, no shortcuts.\n\nOn the fight  rules.\n\nThe time is 3 minutes per fight.\n\nRematch, tap, unpin, movement count, pin count, they all at play, but can be bend upon drivers agreement.\n\nThe bot class are\n\nFairy full combat and sportsman are all in one\n\nAnt plastic full combat\n\nAnd plastic sportsman\n\nAnt full combat\n\nAnt sportsman \n\nBeetle full combat\n\nBeetle sportsman \n\nBut at the end of the day if agreed you can fight  any way you want.\n\nThere will be trophies to the favorite  of the event, sportsmanship, most destructive, and most destroyed.\n\nCome and enjoy the sport just to learn, just to share, just to show.\n\nSeveral arenas are set up on the spot two are safe for all the classes, the others are just Ant full combat and below.",
