    {
      "id": "6131",
      "name": "Olympia Tournament \u0026 Joust",
      "url": "https://www.robotcombatevents.com/events/6131",
      "start_date": "02/28/2026",
      "end_date": "02/28/2026",
      "location": "Olympia, WA, United States",
      "bots_count": 58,
      "logo_url": "https://robotcombatevents.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/event/logo/6131/OlyRobots_Tournament__2_.png",
      "description": "Back for our fourth year!\n\nWe will be running Beetles and Ants as separate events at opposite ends of the commons.\n\n\nTournament \u0026 Joust is Sponsored by\n\nPalm Beach Bots\n\n\n \n\nOlyRobots: Combat Division is sponsored by\n\nFabworks\n\nDiscount: 5% (up to $250 per order) with code OLYROBOTS\n\n\nThe event will be in the school's Commons, please park on the Carlyon side of campus. The North St entrance will be locked.\n\n\n\t0830     Registration \u0026 Pits Open\n\t0900     Safety/Driver Meeting\n\t0930     First Match\n\n\nEvent Details:\n\n\n\tArenas\n\t\n\t\tAnt Weight \u0026 Plastic Ants will be using the 5'x7' WAR arena with a pit\n\t\tBeetleweights will be using the WAR 8'x8' arena\n\t\n\t\n\tThe $20 team registration fee will directly support OlyRobots, the school's FTC \u0026 Combat Robot team. OSPI has stopped providing the grants that used to supported our team. \n\tOur event will be following the SPARC ruleset, which can be found here: https://sparc.tools/ \n\t\n\t\tFor robot construction, please use v1.6\n\t\n\t\n\tTeams will be allowed to register 1 robot in each class to start with, you may register more robots, but they will be waitlisted.\n\tTop robot in each class will be presented with a 3\" pewter medallion\n\tOur 3D Design \u0026 Fabrication class and Maker's Guild are developing a new jousting game, it'll be great\n\tWe will have pizza lunch and concessions available Pizza lunch is $5 cash for two slices of pizza and a drink.\n\n\nLive Streaming:\n\n\n\tWe will be improving our audio situation as we strive to make a better stream. \n\n\n\nBrackets (hidden until we start competition):\n\n\n\tPlastic Ants\n\tAntweight \n\tBeetleweight \n\n\n\n \n\nIn Partnership with Western Allied Robotics",
