      "bots_count": 24,
      "logo_url": "https://robotcombatevents.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/event/logo/6428/AIME_robotronica_banner.png",
      "description": "The American Institute of Mechatronics Engineers Club is hosting it's third annual mechatronics engineering fair, Robotronica! \n\nThe fair is intended to be an educational and fun experience for incoming students at Chico State and the College of Engineering. Robotronica will also feature: capstone projects, robotics booths, and food. \n\nThe main event of this robotics fair will be full combat 1lb, 3lb fights, and 12lb / 15lb robot demos within our new 3/8\" thick polycarbonate 6ft x 6ft arena! This is also the perfect event to showcase non-combat-related projects or tables with heavyweights. Please contact us if you'd like a booth! Current Showcases:\n\nMore to come!\n\nRules:\n\n\n\t\nSPARC ruleset with the following points of emphasis:\n\tFLAMETHROWERS ALLOWED!!\n\tSafety inspection must be completed by 10 AM\n\tExposed batteries are automatic forfeits\n\t\nOne unstick per fight \n\tNo entanglements (nets, tethers, etc)\n\tTapouts are allowed\n\tMatch length: 3 minutes\n\tDouble Elimination with a single final \n\tEvent Livestreamed by AIME\n\tTables and Chairs will be provided\n\t Prizes (Coming soon)\n\tGrudge matches are welcome!\n\tWedge bots welcome!\n\n\nSchedule (Subject to Change):\n\n\n\t 9:00 am: Doors Open / Safety Opens\n\t 9:30 am: Builders Meeting\n\t 10:00 am: Safety Closes and Fights Begin!\n\t12:30 pm: Lunch Break (12/15lb Demos)\n\t1:00 pm: Fights Continue\n\t4:30 pm: Awards and Closing\n\n\nThings to Bring:\n\n\n\tspare parts and tools\n\teye protection\n\tear protection\n\tExtension cords\n\n\nAttendees:\n\n\n\tUnder 18 must be accompanied by parents or guardians\n\tAnyone is welcome to attend - entrance into our facility constitutes acceptance of the informed consent and media release.  The \n\tAdditional Safety Rules regarding batteries (to be finalized) \n\t\n\t\tSafety glasses are required in the pits and while charging, installing or removing batteries. \n\t\tAll batteries must be charged in LiPo bags or other fireproof container\n\t\tBatteries can only be installed for testing or match purposes only \n\t\tBatteries must be removed from the robot as soon as the match is over\n\t\n\t\n\tCompetitors must register before the event to ensure competition slots\n\t\n\t\tyou should contact the event organizer about last-minute registrations\n\t\tadditional registration will be taken in order of waitlist\n\t\tPlease check with event organizers for unique or unusual designs and their application to the linked rulesets\n\t\n\t\n\n\n \n\nLocation: Chico State Arts and Humanities Courtyard (email will be sent with directions to courtyard)",
