      "description": "- Welcome to Philly's first combat robotics competition at Philadelphia Maker Faire 2026 -\n\nHosting 1lb Plastic Ant \u0026 150g Fairyweights\n\nRules:\n\nSPARC regulations:\n\n     - No fire weapons!\n\n     - Referee ruling is final \n\n     - PLANT: only PLA/PLA+/ABS, only drivetrain components can be TPU (where it doesn't act as body armor), battery/battery wire exposure results in automatic forfeit\n\n     - Matches will be 2 minutes long, one unstick per match, one match delay (max 15 minutes) per tournament, test box available (no testing weapons outside box/arena or will lead to disqualification)\n\n     - Arena will be 8x8x2 feet, double pane 1/4\" PC panels with wooden floors\n\n     - Registration begins Feb 28th at noon\n\nEntry Limits: One driver per bot, no more than 2 bots per class/team. 16 teams total for PLANT (if we have more we will increase)\n\nRegistration: $25 per bot, payment due on site (please bring cash)\n\nEvent Passes: Each team is allocated 2 passes to the whole event, free parking for whole day available if you come early before 9AM\n\n \n\nSchedule:\n\nSunday April 19th\n\n8:30AM to 9:30AM: Safety inspection (if you plan to arrive the day before or are in the area, we may open up a time slot if there is enough demand)\n\n9:45AM: Driver's meeting\n\n10AM to 12PM: Fight Robots Fight\n\n12:30PM to 1:30PM: Rest\n\n1PM to 3PM: Fights\n\n \n\nBracket: (PLEASE NOTE: BRACKET NOT FINALIZED, WILL BE RANDOMIZED ON SITE AFTER REGISTRATION IN FRONT OF PARTICIPANTS)\n\nPLAnt (double elimination): TBD\n\nFairyweight (round robin): TBD\n\n \n\nPrizes:\n\nPLANT \u0026 Fairyweight each:\n\n1st Place: TBD\n\n2nd Place: PINECIL Smart mini portable soldering iron\n\n3rd Place: TPU (95A) rainbow filament or Prusament PLA\n\n \n\nVolunteer opportunities are available, please inquire to makerwrangler@phillymakerfaire.com\n\nFeel free to ask questions using the email above, especially if you are a creative robot maker. \n\nGo Birds\n\nEvent updated as of December 8th 2025.",
      "competitions": [
