    {
      "id": "6602",
      "name": "BotRumble - Overture RMRRF '26 PLAnt Tournament - Sunday",
      "url": "https://www.robotcombatevents.com/events/6602",
      "start_date": "04/19/2026",
      "end_date": "04/19/2026",
      "location": "Loveland, CO, United States",
      "bots_count": 0,
      "logo_url": "https://robotcombatevents.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/event/logo/6602/RCE_Logo__New_-_Square_.png",
      "description": "We are thrilled to be back at Rockymountain RepRap Festival 2026 with more robot combat sponsored by Overture Filament! Please read this information carefully to learn how you can smash some robots with us! \n\nWe are running two separate tournaments, one on Saturday and one on Sunday, with 16 competitors in a double elimination format. You may only compete one day, please plan accordingly for the day you pick.  Registration is open to 18 entries but only the first 16 are guaranteed a spot with the remaining two being alternates. Robots must comply with the Sparc 1.6 rules found here - https://sparc.tools/SPARC_Robot_Construction_Specifications_v1.6.pdf. Detailed here is rules for just about any robot design you can imagine, please pay special attention to section 16.3 towards the bottom for details on what materials are allowed. Look over these rules carefully as robots that do not comply with these rules will not be allowed to compete. Additionally, to ensure that we can complete the tournaments each day we can only guarantee 20 minutes between fights, bringing spare parts and tools is highly recommended.\n\nWe will be using Discord as our primary platform for all communication regarding this event. Here you can ask any questions regarding rules, meet other talented builders and most importantly view announcements to upcoming matches during the event itself. It is strongly advised you join to have the best information before and during the event! - https://discord.botrumble.com\n\nWhen: Sunday April 19, 2026\n\nWhere: The Ranch Events Complex -  5280 Arena Cir, Loveland, CO 80538\n\n🛠️ Weight Class\n\n1lb Plastic Antweights (must follow SPARC 16.3 Plastic Class Rule)\n\n💵 Registration\n\nSuggested donation - $5 \n\nPrepay at PayPal here or bring cash/check \n📆 Event Schedule\n\nCheck In and Safety: 9:00-10:00am\n\nMandatory Safety Briefing : 10:00-10:15am\n\nMatches Begin: 10:15AM\n\n🏟️ Arena\n\nAnt\n6' x 6' x 4' \n2 layers of 1/4\" polycarbonate and a 1/8\" polycarbonate kick plate\nWood floor painted with anti-slip paint (https://www.behr.com/consumer/products/floor-coatings-sealers-and-prep/porch-and-patio-floor-paints/porch-patio-anti-slip-floor-paint)\nNo hazards or pits\n🏁 Tournament Format\n\nDouble Elimination\n🧑‍🤝‍🧑 Spectators\n\nWe love spectators! Bring your friends, family, and anyone curious about robot fighting.\n\n📢 Contact\n\nFor more information or questions please join our Discord at https://discord.botrumble.com or find us on Facebook",
      "competitions": [
        {
          "id": "7280",
          "name": "1lb Plastic Antweight",
          "weight_class": "1lb - Plastic Antweight",
