      "bots_count": 0,
      "logo_url": "https://robotcombatevents.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/event/logo/6563/RSL_Event_May_16__1_.png",
      "description": "We are excited to host another MRCA qualifying combat robot competition at the National Guard Armory in Hastings, MN! This event will feature the following weight classes:\n\n\n\t1lb Plastic Antweight\n\t1lb Antweight\n\t3lb Beetleweight\n\n\nAll matches will take place in enclosed arenas to keep the action safe but exciting.\n\nSign Ups\n\nWe will not have caps for sign up for this event. However, to ensure we have enough space planned we will not exceed 120 robots.\n\nSign ups open March 19th at 10 AM CST\n\n\nEvent Details\n\n\n\tDate: May 16, 2026\n\tLocation: Hastings National Guard Armory – 3050 MN-316, Hastings, MN 55033\n\tVenue: Plenty of pit space with provided tables and chairs. TVs will be available to watch fights live.\n\n\nTournament Format\n\nGroup Stage Followed By Single Elimination\n\n\n\t\nGroup Stage: 3 rounds\n\t\nAdvancement: Robots with a 2–1 record or better move on to the Single-Elimination Bracket\n\n\n\nDropping from the Event\n\n\n\tYou may withdraw during the group stage without a forfeit as long as you drop before the next round is published\n\n\tIf you drop in time, you’ll simply be removed from the event\n\n\n\nAfter Group Stage\n\n\n\tWe will start Single Elimination Brackets for each weight class.\n\tOnce all 3 group rounds are complete, open matchmaking will be available\n\n\nOpen Matchmaking\n\nAfter the Group Stage, we’ll open up for matchmaking. How this will work:\n\n\n\tMatches will start with an organized queuing period.\n\n\t\n\t\tInform the Queue Manager when you are ready to be added for matchups\n\t\n\t\n\tRobots are paired against opponents close to their current rank for fair and exciting matches. (For Plastic Ants, this will be random match ups)\n\tRankings are based on MRCA Elo\n\t\n\t\tRobots without an MRCA ranking will start at 1500\n\n\t\tRankings are updated throughout the day\n\n\t\n\t\n\tOnce a match is assigned, it must be fought - withdrawing from an assigned match counts as a forfeit\n\n\t\nQueue limits per driver:\n\t\n\t\tOnly one robot per weight class may be queued at a time. For example: One antweight and one beetleweight may be queued simultaneously, for a single driver.\n\t\tIf you have multiple robots in the same weight class, only one may be queued until its match is completed\n\t\n\t\n\t\nMatchmaking Fees \u0026 Eligibility\n\t\n\t\tOpen matchmaking is included with event registration — there is no additional fee\n\n\t\tAny robot registered for the event may enter matchmaking at any point, including after Group Stage or after eliminated from Single Elimination\n\n\t\tA robot can attend the competition strictly for matchmaking, if this is the case, register your bot under \"Matchmaking Only\"\n\t\n\t\n\n\nIf you have further questions, please email robotsmashingleague@gmail.com.\n\n\n\n\nPlasticAnt Prizes\n\n\n\tWe’ll have trophies for First, Second and Third Place.\n\n\nAnt and Beetleweight Prizes\n\n\n\tWe’ll have trophies for First, Second and Third Place.\n\n\n\nFood\n\n\n\t\nMinne’s on Glenwood – Sliders, Chicago Dogs, Street Polish\n\tEl Huarache Food Truck – Variety of authentic Mexican options\n\n\n\nSponsors\n\nBAIS219 Laser and Machining Services is once again providing the trophies for this event. They specialize in custom machining solutions for one-of-a-kind projects.\n\n\nArena Specs\n\n\n\t\nBeetleweight Arena: 8’ x 8’, painted plywood floor\n\t\nAntweight Arena: 6’ x 6’, painted plywood floor\n\n\n\nSchedule\n\n\n\t8:00 AM – Doors Open for Competitors and Safety Opens\n\t9:45 AM - Drivers’ Meeting\n\t10:00 AM – Spectators Welcome / Group Stage Fights Begin\n\t2:00 PM - Matchmaking Opens \u0026 Single Elimination Brackets Start\n\n\n\nEntry Fees\n\n\n\tFirst entry per driver: $35\n\tAdditional entries: $25\n\tYouth competitors: $25 per entry (flat rate)\n\n\nYou can pay ahead of time via Paypal or Venmo. Just include the name of your bot in the notes. Otherwise feel free to pay day of. \n\n\nRuleset\n\n\n\tThis event will follow MRCA rules and building requirements for Ants \u0026 Beetles. For Plastic Ants the SPARC construction rules will apply.\n\n\n\nSpectators and Volunteers\n\n\n\tSpectators: Free entry, doors open at 10 AM\n\tLive Stream: The event will NOT be fully broadcasted live. We will start a live stream around 2:00 for the single elimination bracket.\n\tVolunteers: Email robotsmashingleague@gmail.com if interested\n\n\n\nStay Connected\n\n\n\tSubscribe to our YouTube Channel for livestreams and videos after the event\n\tEmail robotsmashingleague@gmail.com with any questions",
      "competitions": [
